{{/* Nothing is actually served here — this fragment exists only so Caddy
     obtains and renews a cert for the shared mail server's own hostname
     (HTTP-01, same as every other operator FQDN). mksrv copies the resulting
     cert + key into docker-mailserver's TLS mount (ADR 0032).

     The root-domain hostname stays first in the address list below: Caddy's
     certmagic cache names the cert directory after a site's first configured
     host, and reconcileMailTLS (mail_hosting.go) looks the cert up by that
     exact name — reordering these would break that lookup even though the
     resulting cert (one cert, multiple SANs) still covers every name in the
     list either way.

     .MailBrandedHostnames appends "mail.<domain>" for every tenant that
     opted into mail.branded_hostname (ADR 0032 opt-out) — one shared,
     multi-SAN cert, no per-tenant cert/SNI plumbing needed in
     docker-mailserver itself, which still just gets ONE manual cert file. */}}
mail.{{ .Endpoints.RootDomain }}{{ range .MailBrandedHostnames }}, {{ . }}{{ end }} {
	respond "mksrv mail server" 200
}
